Next is queue_push, which adds an element to the end of the queue. I need to ensure that this operation is thread-safe, so I'll lock the mutex before modifying the list and unlock it after.

```c
void queue_push(Queue* q, int data) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&q->mutex);

    Node* new_node = (Node*)malloc(sizeof(Node));
    if (!new_node) {
        // Memory allocation failed
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&q->mutex);
        return;
    }

    new_node->data = data;
    new_node->next = NULL;

    if (q->rear == NULL) {
        q->front = new_node;
        q->rear = new_node;
